  "id": "source-language",
  "term": "source language",
  "definition": "In bilingual processing and interpreting, the source language is the original language being read or understood before producing another language. Its wording and sentence structure can influence how the target language is produced, sometimes helping when structures match and sometimes causing errors when they do not.",
